- So this Then is a pure observation-and-compare step: it must NOT run the command again and must NOT compute the double itself (no `2 * state.Number`, no arithmetic on `state.Number` at all). The product owns the result; this step only compares what the product printed with the number the Scenario states.
- The engine's pattern is `\Athe result is ((?:[0-9]+|no))\z`, so the single capture may be the word `no` for zero. Mirror the sibling Given (`phrase7c9635...`), which already maps `no` to `0`, so both phrases read the same vocabulary the same way.

